WEBVTT

00:00:27.374 --> 00:00:29.507
- Aah!
- Oh! Oh, sorry.

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:31.596
Oh, Goopy. Aw, it's okay.

00:00:31.639 --> 00:00:35.208
Hey, Federov, you know you can
replicate a larger towel, right?

00:00:35.252 --> 00:00:37.254
It's not his fault.
We're all packed in here.

00:00:37.297 --> 00:00:39.343
Yeah, I love the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos,&lt;/i&gt;
but it's a workhorse.

00:00:39.386 --> 00:00:41.432
It definitely wasn't designed
for all this crew.

00:00:41.475 --> 00:00:43.260
Usually I don't mind the lack
of personal space,

00:00:43.303 --> 00:00:45.349
but recently
it's been too chaotic.

00:00:45.392 --> 00:00:46.785
I don't know,
I think it's kind of fun.

00:00:46.828 --> 00:00:48.439
We're in the middle
of the action, you know?

00:00:48.482 --> 00:00:50.397
We're getting our hands dirty,
even when we sleep.

00:00:50.441 --> 00:00:51.790
-  Huh?

00:00:51.833 --> 00:00:54.923
- I am Minooki.

00:00:54.967 --> 00:00:57.578
Oh, boy, we got a ancient mask
situation here.

00:00:57.622 --> 00:00:58.884
The what now?

00:00:58.927 --> 00:00:59.580
This is, like,
the third time it's happened.

00:00:59.624 --> 00:01:01.147
Stop touching masks.

00:01:01.191 --> 00:01:04.411
I will rebuild my palace.

00:01:04.455 --> 00:01:07.240
- No, no, no. Captain!
- Zenrox, tilling his fields.

00:01:07.284 --> 00:01:08.937
- In the spring. The spring!

00:01:08.981 --> 00:01:12.202
- You cannot contain Minooki.
- Captain!

00:01:12.245 --> 00:01:13.855
- Jerna, before the dawn!
- Captain!

00:01:13.899 --> 00:01:15.596
Oh, yeah, it's super fun
to be in the action.

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:17.816
I just tuned that.

00:02:26.754 --> 00:02:29.322
&lt;i&gt;Captain's log:
once again, the&lt;/i&gt; Cerritos

00:02:29.366 --> 00:02:31.672
&lt;i&gt;was partially transformed
into a temple&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:31.716 --> 00:02:35.546
&lt;i&gt;while I was inhabited
by the spirit of Minooki.&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:35.589 --> 00:02:37.461
&lt;i&gt;Starfleet has to come up
with a better way&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:37.504 --> 00:02:40.203
&lt;i&gt;to handle these D'Arsay
archive situations.&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:40.246 --> 00:02:41.769
&lt;i&gt;Lieutenant Commander Billups
and his engineers&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:41.813 --> 00:02:43.684
&lt;i&gt;have been working
around the clock&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:43.728 --> 00:02:46.992
&lt;i&gt;to repair the systems that
turned into vines and aqueducts,&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:47.035 --> 00:02:48.602
&lt;i&gt;and I'm worried&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:48.646 --> 00:02:51.214
&lt;i&gt;the additional work
has taken an emotional toll.&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:51.257 --> 00:02:53.303
Well, it's taken some time,

00:02:53.346 --> 00:02:55.261
but we've removed
all the sacrificial altars

00:02:55.305 --> 00:02:56.828
from the essential systems,

00:02:56.871 --> 00:02:59.787
and the ship is almost clear
of the crazy mess you made.

00:02:59.831 --> 00:03:02.442
Uh, that Minooki made.

00:03:02.486 --> 00:03:06.577
Right, right, of course. Sorry.
It's been a long day.

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:08.274
You've been working
for a week straight.

00:03:08.318 --> 00:03:09.928
Oh, have I?

00:03:09.971 --> 00:03:12.887
Well, I guess time's
lost all meaning.

00:03:12.931 --> 00:03:15.847
Dr. T'Ana's raised some
concerns, Lieutenant Commander.

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:17.892
Her medical opinion
is that you are

00:03:17.936 --> 00:03:20.068
"a [bleep]ing pile of stress."

00:03:20.112 --> 00:03:22.201
I'm fine! The doc just
needs to stay in her lane,

00:03:22.245 --> 00:03:23.420
'cause I don't go down
to her sickbay

00:03:23.463 --> 00:03:25.465
and tell her
how to hypo her sprays.

00:03:25.509 --> 00:03:27.250
I've been leaning on your team

00:03:27.293 --> 00:03:28.990
pretty hard the last month,

00:03:29.034 --> 00:03:31.036
and we've got this huge project
with the &lt;i&gt;Carlsbad&lt;/i&gt; coming up.

00:03:31.079 --> 00:03:33.256
Ho-ho. More work. Great.

00:03:33.299 --> 00:03:34.735
You can admit
when you need a break.

00:03:34.779 --> 00:03:36.171
It's not a sign of weakness.

00:03:36.215 --> 00:03:37.564
I'm not weak!

00:03:37.608 --> 00:03:39.566
- Ugh.

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:41.481
Let it all out.

00:03:41.525 --> 00:03:43.527
This little breakdown

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:47.400
is exactly why I arranged
a therapeutic getaway

00:03:47.444 --> 00:03:49.272
for you and your team.

00:03:49.315 --> 00:03:52.013
- A-a getaway?
- That's right. Captain's orders.

00:03:52.057 --> 00:03:54.929
Now, who's ready for the most
relaxing mandatory vacation

00:03:54.973 --> 00:03:56.583
of their lives?

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:01.545
You're bringing
a tricorder instruction manual

00:04:01.588 --> 00:04:03.547
- on your spa trip?
- Aah!

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:04.983
Yeah, something fun to read

00:04:05.026 --> 00:04:06.550
in case
all the relaxing gets boring.

00:04:06.593 --> 00:04:08.334
Mm. I better take two.

00:04:08.378 --> 00:04:10.336
With the captain gone,
we're just gonna have to be

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:12.338
in standby, so you won't be
missing out on much here.

00:04:12.382 --> 00:04:13.818
Well, there's the room lottery.

00:04:13.861 --> 00:04:15.341
Oh, right.
I forgot that was coming up.

00:04:15.385 --> 00:04:17.430
Four separate quarters
opened up on Deck One.

00:04:17.474 --> 00:04:19.737
Deck One?
Those are the penthouse suites.

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:22.348
I could fit
so many beakers in there.

00:04:22.392 --> 00:04:24.524
The next time Captain's
possessed by a haunted mask,

00:04:24.568 --> 00:04:26.396
I could just close the door.

00:04:26.439 --> 00:04:27.440
So I am missing out.

00:04:27.484 --> 00:04:28.920
Don't worry about it, man.

00:04:28.963 --> 00:04:30.574
We'll enter your name
into the lottery.

00:04:30.617 --> 00:04:32.053
Not like it'll matter.
Room lottery has always been

00:04:32.097 --> 00:04:33.533
weighted for higher stations.

00:04:33.577 --> 00:04:35.187
Lower deckers don't end up
in fancy rooms.

00:04:35.230 --> 00:04:36.580
Who knows?
Maybe we'll get lucky.

00:04:36.623 --> 00:04:38.277
-  Aah!

00:04:38.321 --> 00:04:41.367
- I'm sorry.
- Goopy! Get back here.

00:04:48.461 --> 00:04:49.854
It'll be super easy.

00:04:49.897 --> 00:04:51.812
: Delta shift.

00:04:51.856 --> 00:04:53.510
We access the terminal
on Deck Nine,

00:04:53.553 --> 00:04:55.381
change a few lines of code,
then the stupid

00:04:55.425 --> 00:04:57.514
lottery algorithm
will have to pick us.

00:04:57.557 --> 00:04:59.994
Uh, but what about
the turbolift records?

00:05:00.038 --> 00:05:01.518
We're gonna get caught.

00:05:01.561 --> 00:05:03.520
Not if we go in the back way.

00:05:03.563 --> 00:05:04.782
There's no active monitoring

00:05:04.825 --> 00:05:06.261
in the auxiliary corridors.

00:05:06.305 --> 00:05:07.959
We'll be untraceable.

00:05:08.002 --> 00:05:10.701
You're right.
Deck One, here we come.

00:05:13.747 --> 00:05:15.923
Ugh.

00:05:15.967 --> 00:05:17.403
And then they all laughed

00:05:17.447 --> 00:05:19.449
in that mean,
Delta shift way they do.

00:05:19.492 --> 00:05:20.972
Ugh. Delta shift's the worst.

00:05:21.015 --> 00:05:22.408
How are they even in Starfleet?

00:05:22.452 --> 00:05:24.105
They should all just
join the Maquis.

00:05:24.149 --> 00:05:25.977
Well, those jerks figured out
how to rig the lottery

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:27.674
using an air-gapped terminal.

00:05:27.718 --> 00:05:30.068
Oh, they're definitely getting
those Deck One rooms.

00:05:30.111 --> 00:05:31.765
No, no way. No, we got
to get to that terminal

00:05:31.809 --> 00:05:33.463
and beat them
at their own game.

00:05:33.506 --> 00:05:35.378
But isn't that... cheating?

00:05:35.421 --> 00:05:36.988
So is the whole room lottery.

00:05:37.031 --> 00:05:38.729
Look, after all the times
we've been cheated,

00:05:38.772 --> 00:05:40.687
we'll just be
evening things out.

00:05:40.731 --> 00:05:42.559
And if we don't do something,
they will.

00:05:42.602 --> 00:05:45.344
Ooh, I've always wanted
to explore an ethical gray area.

00:05:45.388 --> 00:05:49.566
Yes! Let's go gray area
the [bleep] out of Delta shift.

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:05.016
Ah, Captain Freeman
and her engineers.

00:06:05.059 --> 00:06:07.148
Welcome to the &lt;i&gt;Dove.&lt;/i&gt;

00:06:07.192 --> 00:06:10.500
I'm Toz, and my mission
is your relaxation.

00:06:10.543 --> 00:06:12.240
I understand
your department's been

00:06:12.284 --> 00:06:13.981
under some intense pressure.

00:06:14.025 --> 00:06:15.548
Right, well, you know,
just doing our job,

00:06:15.592 --> 00:06:17.550
so, uh, how long is this
gonna take, anyway?

00:06:17.594 --> 00:06:21.467
Here on the &lt;i&gt;Dove,&lt;/i&gt; we've mastered
the science of relaxation.

00:06:21.511 --> 00:06:23.817
Wrist bands, lemonade.

00:06:23.861 --> 00:06:26.080
These bands monitor
your tension levels,

00:06:26.124 --> 00:06:28.779
so we can adjust your treatment accordingly.

00:06:28.822 --> 00:06:32.043
Yellow indicates you're all
experiencing moderate stress.

00:06:32.086 --> 00:06:35.481
But soon enough, we'll have you
green across the board.

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:40.268
The puppy playpen is one
of our most popular offerings.

00:06:40.312 --> 00:06:43.358
For the more deviant among you,
we also have kittens.

00:06:43.402 --> 00:06:44.838
No judgment.

00:06:44.882 --> 00:06:47.145
Our baths feature mud
imported directly

00:06:47.188 --> 00:06:49.756
from the healing bogs
of Tellar Prime.

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:52.411
Temperature
and viscosity are bespoke.

00:06:52.455 --> 00:06:55.109
Everyone has a different way
of relaxing.

00:06:57.155 --> 00:06:59.462
- Look at the joy on his face.

00:06:59.505 --> 00:07:01.028
He's actually gone
way over his time.

00:07:01.072 --> 00:07:02.726
We're afraid to end his session.

00:07:02.769 --> 00:07:05.772
We can't wait to see
what you have prepared for us.

00:07:05.816 --> 00:07:07.513
Isn't that right, Mr. Billup...?

00:07:07.557 --> 00:07:09.036
Billups, what are you doing?

00:07:09.080 --> 00:07:10.821
Oh, sorry, yeah,

00:07:10.864 --> 00:07:12.257
we noticed that the-the hatch,

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:13.954
uh, the, you know,
the sliding hatch--

00:07:13.998 --> 00:07:15.390
- it wasn't operating at, uh...

00:07:15.434 --> 00:07:17.392
- We fixed the door.

00:07:17.436 --> 00:07:20.134
Hmm. We must begin
the program immediately.

00:07:20.178 --> 00:07:22.223
Here's the terminal room.
The Deltas are going there

00:07:22.267 --> 00:07:24.530
through the auxiliary corridors,
but we can get there faster

00:07:24.574 --> 00:07:26.880
if we cut
through the maintenance systems.

00:07:26.924 --> 00:07:28.882
It's gonna be a hike,
and probably some tight fits,

00:07:28.926 --> 00:07:30.536
but it should
get us there first.

00:07:30.580 --> 00:07:32.538
Hey, I will gladly get
chin-deep in a waste conduit

00:07:32.582 --> 00:07:34.279
if it means beating
those stupid Deltas.

00:07:34.322 --> 00:07:36.194
All right, well, the shortcut
starts through a panel

00:07:36.237 --> 00:07:37.587
in the back of Holodeck Three.

00:07:37.630 --> 00:07:38.892
Ugh, there's a program running.

00:07:38.936 --> 00:07:40.024
I guess we're gonna have

00:07:40.067 --> 00:07:41.416
- to wait it out.
- No time.

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:43.201
Just stay low.

00:07:43.244 --> 00:07:45.246
- Huh. Oh, I know what this is.

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:47.640
I think this is what people used
to use to store their money.

00:07:47.684 --> 00:07:48.989
It's called a bonk?

00:07:49.033 --> 00:07:50.556
Oh, what a boring program.

00:07:50.600 --> 00:07:52.123
:
Uh, yes, hello.

00:07:52.166 --> 00:07:54.560
I'd like to withdraw some paper
with no intrinsic value.

00:07:54.604 --> 00:07:56.562
: Money.

00:07:57.607 --> 00:07:58.651
Aah!

00:07:58.695 --> 00:08:00.000
Everybody down!
This is a robbery!

00:08:00.044 --> 00:08:02.046
Hands up where I can see 'em.

00:08:02.089 --> 00:08:05.179
I didn't wake up today planning
on blowing anyone's brains out,

00:08:05.223 --> 00:08:06.703
but don't push me.

00:08:08.226 --> 00:08:10.054
Son of a...
Oh, [bleep], it's the Feds!

00:08:10.097 --> 00:08:11.882
- Over here. &lt;i&gt;
- You're surrounded!&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:11.925 --> 00:08:13.579
T'ANA:
Bring it, scumbags.

00:08:13.623 --> 00:08:15.146
We're not scared of you!

00:08:15.189 --> 00:08:16.277
- Aah!

00:08:18.323 --> 00:08:21.065
Computer, deactivate
safety protocols.

00:08:21.108 --> 00:08:23.546
- What?!
- Eat hot lead!

00:08:23.589 --> 00:08:26.592
- Computer, pause program.

00:08:29.073 --> 00:08:30.727
Aah! Mm.

00:08:30.770 --> 00:08:32.598
What the hell?!
I was about to blast 'em.

00:08:32.642 --> 00:08:34.469
What are we doing?

00:08:34.513 --> 00:08:37.429
The usual: we off these Feds,
and once our blood's pumping,

00:08:37.472 --> 00:08:38.865
we'll do the nasty
on the counter

00:08:38.909 --> 00:08:41.520
- and make the hostages watch.
- Aw, geez.

00:08:41.564 --> 00:08:43.000
No, I mean
what are we doing,

00:08:43.043 --> 00:08:44.044
- as a couple?
- Ew, just shoot me instead.

00:08:44.088 --> 00:08:44.915
What are you talking about?

00:08:44.958 --> 00:08:46.133
You love crime play.

00:08:46.177 --> 00:08:47.091
When was the last time

00:08:47.134 --> 00:08:48.614
you asked me about my dreams?

00:08:48.658 --> 00:08:50.485
Or how my mission went?
I died,

00:08:50.529 --> 00:08:53.097
and we never even
talked about it.

00:08:53.140 --> 00:08:55.055
Does baby need to suckle
on one of mama's...

00:08:55.099 --> 00:08:56.404
- Will you put those away, Diane?
- Ugh.

00:08:56.448 --> 00:08:58.493
- Diane is her kinky sex name?
- This is worse

00:08:58.537 --> 00:09:00.234
- than the shootout.
- I am more than a rock-hard body

00:09:00.278 --> 00:09:01.932
- for you to scramble around on.
- Okay, we have to go.

00:09:01.975 --> 00:09:03.368
- Got it.
- I want us to share

00:09:03.411 --> 00:09:04.848
- our feelings, our secrets.
- In here.

00:09:04.891 --> 00:09:07.024
Okay, bigs,
I'll tell you a secret.

00:09:07.067 --> 00:09:09.635
It's something I would &lt;i&gt;kill&lt;/i&gt;
if anyone else ever knew.

00:09:09.679 --> 00:09:10.897
Oh, God, hurry, hurry.

00:09:10.941 --> 00:09:13.204
I've never told anyone
how I lost my tail.

00:09:13.247 --> 00:09:14.640
Oh, yes.

00:09:14.684 --> 00:09:15.989
- Tendi, come on.
- No, no, no.

00:09:16.033 --> 00:09:17.382
I've always wanted to know.

00:09:17.425 --> 00:09:19.645
Hey, can we, uh, set the mood?

00:09:19.689 --> 00:09:21.429
Computer, resume program.

00:09:21.473 --> 00:09:23.127
- T'ANA: I was on the &lt;i&gt;Algonquin.&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:23.170 --> 00:09:25.477
Aah! Aw, man.

00:09:32.440 --> 00:09:34.225
&lt;i&gt;All right,
we're making great time.&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:34.268 --> 00:09:35.661
No way is Delta shift beating us
to that terminal.

00:09:35.705 --> 00:09:37.228
They better not.
This is taking forever.

00:09:37.271 --> 00:09:38.925
Well, I think the view

00:09:38.969 --> 00:09:40.797
from our new quarters
will more than make up for it.

00:09:40.840 --> 00:09:43.016
Plus, we're in parts of the
ship almost nobody gets to see.

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:45.018
I think this is super cool.

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:49.283
Ugh. [gags] Ugh.

00:09:49.327 --> 00:09:51.721
Uh, if by super cool
you mean super gross.

00:09:51.764 --> 00:09:53.679
Why do we even
have a swamp on board?

00:09:53.723 --> 00:09:55.246
We're under the hydroponics bay.

00:09:55.289 --> 00:09:56.726
It's great
for biomedical research,

00:09:56.769 --> 00:09:58.162
or just for flower fans.

00:09:58.205 --> 00:09:59.642
What kind of weirdo signs up

00:09:59.685 --> 00:10:01.905
for a job
in outer space just to garden?

00:10:03.254 --> 00:10:05.648
Ah, the path to Kamata
in spring.

00:10:05.691 --> 00:10:07.693
Whoop. Oh, Gramble,

00:10:07.737 --> 00:10:10.653
his throat slit
by his mistress.

00:10:13.177 --> 00:10:14.874
A Tamarian defrin root.

00:10:14.918 --> 00:10:16.484
They can grow without water.

00:10:16.528 --> 00:10:18.399
All they need is high levels
of nitrous oxide.

00:10:18.443 --> 00:10:20.532
Uh, is it safe for us
to be breathing that?

00:10:20.575 --> 00:10:22.577
Oh. Well, I know
Orions are immune

00:10:22.621 --> 00:10:23.840
to its hallucinogenic properties.

00:10:23.883 --> 00:10:26.843
:
But as for humans...

00:10:26.886 --> 00:10:28.801
Um...

00:10:28.845 --> 00:10:30.629
Boimler, what is up
with your head?

00:10:30.673 --> 00:10:32.718
You look like
a goddamn sea creature.

00:10:34.372 --> 00:10:38.463
My head? What about your arms?

00:10:38.506 --> 00:10:40.900
Yeah, I mean,
I don't hate it, though.

00:10:40.944 --> 00:10:43.642
Hey, guys, this is actually
so funny. Look at this.

00:10:43.686 --> 00:10:47.167
It says oxygen levels
are depleting.

00:10:47.211 --> 00:10:50.257
I can taste sounds? What?

00:10:50.301 --> 00:10:51.998
:
We have to get out of here.

00:10:54.174 --> 00:10:57.134
BOIMLER [echoing]:
How? It's a maze.

00:10:57.177 --> 00:10:58.962
What? What...

00:10:59.005 --> 00:11:00.441
- what maze?
- Okay,

00:11:00.485 --> 00:11:02.052
you guys stay here
and feed the rabbits.

00:11:02.095 --> 00:11:03.662
I'm gonna find a way
through this maze.

00:11:03.706 --> 00:11:06.491
- No! What?!
- I am trapped inside of an egg.

00:11:06.534 --> 00:11:08.145
- Come on.
- No, leave me alone.

00:11:08.188 --> 00:11:09.929
- I don't want to hatch.
- Ooh, I've found the door.

00:11:09.973 --> 00:11:11.801
- Ugh. We have to go. Now.
- No, I do.

00:11:14.238 --> 00:11:16.066
- Ow!

00:11:16.109 --> 00:11:17.894
- I said go! Hyah! Hyah!

00:11:17.937 --> 00:11:19.896
- Why are you being so mean? Ow.

00:11:23.987 --> 00:11:26.729
Whew. Sorry-sorry
about that whole egg thing.

00:11:26.772 --> 00:11:29.383
That's okay.
I'm sorry I made you hatch.

00:11:30.428 --> 00:11:33.170
It's okay. It's just,
oh, it was so warm in there.

00:11:34.214 --> 00:11:38.001
Ooh, that Tellarite mud bath
was phenomenal.

00:11:38.044 --> 00:11:40.264
I'm glad you enjoyed it,
and even more pleased

00:11:40.307 --> 00:11:43.658
to see your team taking full
advantage of our sand garden.

00:11:43.702 --> 00:11:47.097
Feeling your stress
slide away into the sand?

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:49.186
Oh, yeah.
Oh, we're really cookin'.

00:11:49.229 --> 00:11:51.362
Oh, nice. Wait a minute.

00:11:51.405 --> 00:11:53.190
Is that a design schematic?

00:11:53.233 --> 00:11:55.235
Yup. This little honey
will improve the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt;

00:11:55.279 --> 00:11:57.760
engine efficiency by .5%.

00:11:57.803 --> 00:11:58.804
No. No, no, no, no, no.

00:11:58.848 --> 00:12:00.763
You are here to relax.

00:12:00.806 --> 00:12:03.461
Like, look.
Meredith's got the right idea.

00:12:03.504 --> 00:12:06.812
Mmm. Right there.
That's the spot.

00:12:06.856 --> 00:12:09.162
Ensign, working out
all those kinks?

00:12:09.206 --> 00:12:11.382
Oh, yeah, it's just about ready
to get tested.

00:12:11.425 --> 00:12:14.907
I'm sorry. Excuse me?
Ugh. This is unbelievable.

00:12:14.951 --> 00:12:16.866
Sorry. Was I the only one
sneaking in a little build time?

00:12:16.909 --> 00:12:18.737
FREEMAN [muttering]: They won't
relax. Why won't they relax?

00:12:18.781 --> 00:12:21.044
This is ridiculous.

00:12:21.087 --> 00:12:22.959
I'm all for adventure, Boims,
but it'd be nice

00:12:23.002 --> 00:12:25.744
if your little shortcut wasn't
actually more of a long cut.

00:12:25.788 --> 00:12:27.833
Look, I know, I know. It's just,
after all these retrofits,

00:12:27.877 --> 00:12:29.835
a lot of this stuff
isn't even labeled.

00:12:29.879 --> 00:12:32.446
I mean, like this.
Uh, ladies first?

00:12:32.490 --> 00:12:33.665
- Absolutely not.
- Yeah, right.

00:12:33.708 --> 00:12:35.188
Cool, cool. I got this.

00:12:37.538 --> 00:12:40.846
- Holy cow.
- Ooh!

00:12:40.890 --> 00:12:43.196
Whoa. Check it out.
Gravity's super low.

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:44.807
Ha, ha. Okay.

00:12:44.850 --> 00:12:47.113
- This is a much better room.

00:12:47.157 --> 00:12:48.941
All right, Boims,
I'll give you this one.

00:12:48.985 --> 00:12:51.117
This is a good shortcut. Ooh.

00:12:53.598 --> 00:12:55.252
- Oh, look at me go.
- Whoa.

00:12:55.295 --> 00:12:56.775
Feels so free to do
this without an EV suit.

00:12:56.819 --> 00:12:58.821
- Come on, Boimler.

00:12:58.864 --> 00:13:00.605
Delta shift probably isn't
goofing off like this.

00:13:00.648 --> 00:13:02.433
We got to go
if we want to beat them.

00:13:02.476 --> 00:13:05.131
Ha. I'm not Boimler.
I'm Antigrav Boy,

00:13:05.175 --> 00:13:09.570
protector of the lower decks.

00:13:11.964 --> 00:13:14.532
Commander, a small
asteroid cluster is approaching.

00:13:14.575 --> 00:13:16.534
Should I target
with all phasers?

00:13:16.577 --> 00:13:18.928
What? No. This is what
we have a deflector for.

00:13:18.971 --> 00:13:21.582
Reroute power and
let the dish take care of it.

00:13:24.542 --> 00:13:25.717
- Uh-oh. Huh?

00:13:28.720 --> 00:13:29.721
Aah!

00:13:29.764 --> 00:13:31.549
Help me!

00:13:31.592 --> 00:13:34.552
- Whoa!
- Aah!

00:13:36.989 --> 00:13:38.556
He's getting flattened.
We need to make a tether.

00:13:38.599 --> 00:13:40.297
Uh, got it!

00:13:40.340 --> 00:13:42.560
Oh, my God! Oh, no. No!

00:13:42.603 --> 00:13:43.691
Hold on!

00:13:46.259 --> 00:13:50.176
- Ow!
- Mariner, pull!

00:13:50.220 --> 00:13:53.049
- Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow!

00:13:56.139 --> 00:13:57.662
Antigrav Boy.

00:13:59.794 --> 00:14:01.535
&lt;i&gt;
The human ritual&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:01.579 --> 00:14:03.363
of mani-pedis is renowned

00:14:03.407 --> 00:14:06.410
across the quadrant
for its calming power.

00:14:06.453 --> 00:14:08.629
Also, I know it would keep their
eyes covered and hands busy.

00:14:08.673 --> 00:14:10.414
Well, seems like

00:14:10.457 --> 00:14:13.069
you've finally figured out
how to make them relax.

00:14:13.112 --> 00:14:15.680
Not a single yellow
wristband in the bunch.

00:14:15.723 --> 00:14:18.465
Ah. Feeling good,
Mr. Rutherford?

00:14:18.509 --> 00:14:20.119
Oh, yeah, Captain.

00:14:20.163 --> 00:14:22.034
It's about time these
little piggies got pampered.

00:14:22.078 --> 00:14:24.123
If you like that,
you'll love the manicure.

00:14:24.167 --> 00:14:25.995
Oh, just the pedi's fine.

00:14:26.038 --> 00:14:29.215
Come on. You can't have a pedi
without a mani.

00:14:29.259 --> 00:14:31.957
It's like a pedi
for your hand-toes.

00:14:32.001 --> 00:14:34.046
Uh, no, thanks, not for me.

00:14:34.090 --> 00:14:37.136
Wait a minute.
Did you slide a cucumber slice

00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:39.834
under your wristband
to block the sensor?

00:14:39.878 --> 00:14:43.447
You engineered a workaround
to your own stress meter?

00:14:43.490 --> 00:14:45.275
I'm sorry.
We just wanted you to be happy.

00:14:45.318 --> 00:14:48.756
Damn it. Oh. What the hell
were you thinking?

00:14:48.800 --> 00:14:50.715
That the cucumber's hydrophilic
skin creates a natural fil...

00:14:50.758 --> 00:14:52.630
- Can it, Meredith.
- Sorry, Captain.

00:14:52.673 --> 00:14:54.762
We just didn't want our stress
to stress you out.

00:14:54.806 --> 00:14:56.503
This is a direct attack.

00:14:56.547 --> 00:14:58.331
I came here thinking
you respected me enough

00:14:58.375 --> 00:15:01.160
to give it a fair shot,
but no. No!

00:15:01.204 --> 00:15:04.468
- My engineers don't respect me.
- That's not true!

00:15:04.511 --> 00:15:06.513
It's just one deception
after another!

00:15:06.557 --> 00:15:08.646
I must be the worst captain
in the whole freakin' fleet,

00:15:08.689 --> 00:15:10.300
- a total joke.

00:15:10.343 --> 00:15:11.866
- Am I amusing you?

00:15:11.910 --> 00:15:13.303
We have a black bander
on Deck Four.

00:15:13.346 --> 00:15:14.391
- Do I amuse you?
- a black bander on Four.

00:15:14.434 --> 00:15:15.870
This is not a drill.

00:15:15.914 --> 00:15:18.351
Don't touch me! Just stand down.
I am a captain.

00:15:18.395 --> 00:15:19.787
We've been treating
the wrong patient.

00:15:19.831 --> 00:15:21.659
This woman is under
incredible stress.

00:15:21.702 --> 00:15:23.574
She hasn't recently
been possessed

00:15:23.617 --> 00:15:25.054
by any ancient artifacts,
has she?

00:15:25.097 --> 00:15:27.404
Uh... maybe a couple?

00:15:27.447 --> 00:15:29.841
Intensive treatment. Now!

00:15:29.884 --> 00:15:31.408
- Move.
- Oh, engineers. All of them.

00:15:31.451 --> 00:15:33.236
All of them are all
goddamned Geordi LaForges.

00:15:33.279 --> 00:15:34.802
What's gonna happen to her?

00:15:34.846 --> 00:15:37.240
She's been repressing
months' worth of stress,

00:15:37.283 --> 00:15:38.632
and you brought it all out.

00:15:38.676 --> 00:15:40.069
If she doesn't respond
to treatment, I'll have to

00:15:40.112 --> 00:15:42.158
send her to Earth
for a full medical diagnostic.

00:15:42.201 --> 00:15:44.203
But that would take her away
from the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:44.247 --> 00:15:45.813
Something that
could have been avoided

00:15:45.857 --> 00:15:47.815
if you'd just followed
my treatments. But, no,

00:15:47.859 --> 00:15:50.818
you just had
to be hardworking.

00:15:50.862 --> 00:15:54.257
She's right.
We didn't make an effort today.

00:15:54.300 --> 00:15:56.085
If that's what
the captain needs, then we need

00:15:56.128 --> 00:15:58.087
to figure out a way to stop engineering

00:15:58.130 --> 00:16:00.915
- and start relaxing.

00:16:00.959 --> 00:16:04.267
Sir, I think I know
what we shouldn't do.

00:16:08.358 --> 00:16:10.534
This vent opens
for ten seconds once every hour.

00:16:10.577 --> 00:16:12.927
When it does, we'll have a
straight shot to the terminal.

00:16:12.971 --> 00:16:14.538
Great. So what do we do now?

00:16:14.581 --> 00:16:16.627
All we have to do is wait.

00:16:18.063 --> 00:16:20.239
When you get your room, what are
you gonna say to let people in?

00:16:20.283 --> 00:16:22.850
Yeah, Riker says
"Come," but like, "Come."

00:16:22.894 --> 00:16:25.331
So I guess I'll do that?
Do I sound cool? Come.

00:16:25.375 --> 00:16:27.638
I wish I could make fun,
but it does sound cool.

00:16:27.681 --> 00:16:29.727
I was thinking, "Enter, friend."

00:16:29.770 --> 00:16:31.555
So then whoever comes in
is your friend.

00:16:31.598 --> 00:16:33.252
I'm going to say "Come," too.

00:16:33.296 --> 00:16:34.688
No, don't do that. That's mine.

00:16:34.732 --> 00:16:37.213
- I like it. Come. Come.
- Come.

00:16:37.256 --> 00:16:39.693
- Enter, friend.

00:16:39.737 --> 00:16:42.261
- Oh, great.
- Beta shifters?

00:16:42.305 --> 00:16:44.002
What the hell are you freaks
doing down here?

00:16:44.046 --> 00:16:45.395
Same as you, Delta shift.

00:16:45.438 --> 00:16:47.092
What took you so long, huh?

00:16:47.136 --> 00:16:49.399
Tuckered out from staying up
past your bedtimes?

00:16:49.442 --> 00:16:51.096
You know what?
Yeah. We're tired,

00:16:51.140 --> 00:16:52.576
and we've been through hell
to get here.

00:16:52.619 --> 00:16:54.012
I can't believe you're trying

00:16:54.056 --> 00:16:56.188
to bone in
on our room lottery plan.

00:16:56.232 --> 00:16:57.624
Aren't you Beta shifters
always crowing

00:16:57.668 --> 00:16:59.235
about how ethical you are?

00:16:59.278 --> 00:17:01.106
You sure you'll be able
to live with yourselves

00:17:01.150 --> 00:17:03.239
- if you hack that terminal?
- Yeah, I don't know.

00:17:03.282 --> 00:17:04.892
I just feel like
all the Deck One perks

00:17:04.936 --> 00:17:06.677
and privacy'll help us
deal with it.

00:17:06.720 --> 00:17:09.114
Well, we're not going anywhere.

00:17:09.158 --> 00:17:11.725
Yeah. I didn't crawl through
a leftover Minooki aqueduct

00:17:11.769 --> 00:17:13.640
for nothing.
I'm drenched down to my soul.

00:17:13.684 --> 00:17:15.686
At least
you weren't in the holodeck

00:17:15.729 --> 00:17:18.036
for Shaxs' and T'Ana's
foreplay fantasy. Ugh.

00:17:18.080 --> 00:17:19.951
Oh, man, you ran into them, too?

00:17:19.994 --> 00:17:23.433
We heard them going to town
from behind stellar cartography.

00:17:23.476 --> 00:17:25.522
Aw. I knew
they were making progress.

00:17:25.565 --> 00:17:28.351
Yeah, they were definitely
making something.

00:17:28.394 --> 00:17:29.526
- Oh!

00:17:29.569 --> 00:17:30.570
Ew.

00:17:30.614 --> 00:17:32.355
Barf.

00:17:32.398 --> 00:17:35.184
I doubt they'll ever
let Dr. Migleemo choose

00:17:35.227 --> 00:17:36.968
which nebula to scan again
after that.

00:17:37.011 --> 00:17:39.144
Oh, oh, oh, I got a good one.
I got a really good one.

00:17:39.188 --> 00:17:40.928
Remember when Ransom
got turned into a caveman

00:17:40.972 --> 00:17:42.582
and they locked him
in the cafeteria?

00:17:42.626 --> 00:17:44.715
So, apparently,
when he was in there,

00:17:44.758 --> 00:17:47.413
he replicated this weird doll
out of churros

00:17:47.457 --> 00:17:50.112
and carried it around
like it was his wife.

00:17:50.155 --> 00:17:52.723
Everyone knows that.
People called her Churrolivia.

00:17:52.766 --> 00:17:55.682
Okay, but did you know
he still has the doll?

00:17:55.726 --> 00:17:57.423
- Churro, the wife? No.
- Oh! Uh-uh. Oh!

00:17:57.467 --> 00:17:59.686
I heard he keeps it
somewhere in his office

00:17:59.730 --> 00:18:02.298
'cause of like a primordial
bond he has with it.

00:18:02.341 --> 00:18:05.039
It does always smell
like cinnamon in there. Oh, no.

00:18:05.083 --> 00:18:07.041
Come on. That caveman thing
was like six months ago.

00:18:07.085 --> 00:18:09.000
The churros would all be
dried out by now.

00:18:09.043 --> 00:18:11.524
He keeps it... refreshed.

00:18:11.568 --> 00:18:14.397
- Ew!

00:18:14.440 --> 00:18:16.616
You know, we're really not,
like, that different.

00:18:16.660 --> 00:18:19.097
I feel like a big part of why
we haven't gotten along is just,

00:18:19.141 --> 00:18:20.881
you're asleep when we're awake.

00:18:20.925 --> 00:18:23.449
But spending this time together,
it's actually been nice.

00:18:23.493 --> 00:18:25.364
Yeah, you guys are all right.

00:18:25.408 --> 00:18:28.019
Too bad when the vent opens,
we won't have this anymore.

00:18:28.062 --> 00:18:30.674
It would be better if all us
lower deckers stuck together.

00:18:30.717 --> 00:18:33.242
I mean, why don't we? We could
all walk through together.

00:18:33.285 --> 00:18:35.853
Yeah. Put all our names
into the lottery.

00:18:35.896 --> 00:18:37.637
At least it'll make it
an even split.

00:18:37.681 --> 00:18:40.466
I like it. Let us lower deckers
have the luck for once.

00:18:40.510 --> 00:18:42.164
And then no matter
who gets the rooms,

00:18:42.207 --> 00:18:43.817
we come out of it
with new friends.

00:18:43.861 --> 00:18:46.211
Delta shift and Beta shift
working together.

00:18:46.255 --> 00:18:48.039
- Got it! Quick, quick!

00:18:48.082 --> 00:18:49.214
- Nice try, Betas.

00:18:49.258 --> 00:18:51.303
- Delta shift!

00:18:51.347 --> 00:18:53.175
Goddamn you
Delta shift pieces of sh...

00:18:59.355 --> 00:19:01.270
Try-try to do a good thing. Try...

00:19:01.313 --> 00:19:04.229
- Get away from me, dog.
- Oh, this is bad.

00:19:04.273 --> 00:19:06.623
- Increase puppy levels.
- That's all we've got.

00:19:06.666 --> 00:19:09.669
We even tossed in a couple
of bunnies. They had no effect.

00:19:09.713 --> 00:19:11.454
Oh, [bleep].

00:19:12.455 --> 00:19:14.587
I'm gonna call it.

00:19:14.631 --> 00:19:15.762
Somebody get me

00:19:15.806 --> 00:19:17.547
- Starfleet Medical on the horn.
- Stop!

00:19:18.765 --> 00:19:20.637
Aw, not you, little guys.
Keep on puppin'.

00:19:20.680 --> 00:19:23.509
Haven't you done enough damage?
Get out of here!

00:19:23.553 --> 00:19:25.076
Captain, you were right.

00:19:25.119 --> 00:19:26.991
- Letting go of stress is key,

00:19:27.034 --> 00:19:29.472
and we finally figured out how.
Bring it in!

00:19:29.515 --> 00:19:32.039
Did you dismantle one
of my turbolifts?

00:19:32.083 --> 00:19:33.650
We have engineered a machine

00:19:33.693 --> 00:19:36.305
that removes stress.

00:19:36.348 --> 00:19:38.220
You built this? Ugh.

00:19:38.263 --> 00:19:40.918
The whole point of this trip
was to stop working.

00:19:40.961 --> 00:19:43.355
We know, Captain,
but it turns out, for us,

00:19:43.399 --> 00:19:45.052
there is no greater
stress relief

00:19:45.096 --> 00:19:47.707
than engineering a solution
to a problem.

00:19:47.751 --> 00:19:49.709
- No, this is preposterous.

00:19:49.753 --> 00:19:52.451
- Ready the captain for transfer.
- Captain, please.

00:19:52.495 --> 00:19:54.540
Ten seconds in this pod
will give you the same

00:19:54.584 --> 00:19:56.716
therapeutic benefits
of a month spent on the &lt;i&gt;Dove.&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:56.760 --> 00:20:00.154
Will you try it?
We can't afford to lose you.

00:20:01.460 --> 00:20:02.853
Ugh. All right, all right, fine.

00:20:02.896 --> 00:20:05.421
Wait, now, how does this work?

00:20:05.464 --> 00:20:07.118
-  Whoa.

00:20:07.161 --> 00:20:09.294
Ah. Oh! Aah!

00:20:11.818 --> 00:20:13.820
Captain, how do you feel?

00:20:13.864 --> 00:20:16.649
That was... incredible.

00:20:16.693 --> 00:20:18.390
Oh, it was better than

00:20:18.434 --> 00:20:21.393
a thousand massages combined.

00:20:21.437 --> 00:20:24.048
Oh, my God,
I feel like a new woman.

00:20:24.091 --> 00:20:26.659
Remarkable. Your levels have
all returned to baseline.

00:20:26.703 --> 00:20:28.313
What an amazing device.

00:20:28.357 --> 00:20:30.141
With one of these
on every ship,

00:20:30.184 --> 00:20:32.230
Starfleet will no longer
even need the &lt;i&gt;Dove.&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:32.274 --> 00:20:35.668
And you can thank the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt;
engineers for that.

00:20:35.712 --> 00:20:37.670
Come on, team.
Let's get back to work.

00:20:37.714 --> 00:20:40.194
- Yes, work!
-  yeah!

00:20:40.238 --> 00:20:42.371
Oh, yeah. Bye-bye, yeah.

00:20:42.414 --> 00:20:44.895
I want this thing ejected
from my ship right now!

00:20:44.938 --> 00:20:47.811
- But, it's exactly what we...
- I said get rid of it!

00:20:47.854 --> 00:20:49.378
Gah! After everything
we went through,

00:20:49.421 --> 00:20:50.944
- stupid Delta shift won.
- I can't believe

00:20:50.988 --> 00:20:53.077
I laughed
at their caveman Ransom story.

00:20:53.120 --> 00:20:54.818
It's probably fake,
just like they are.

00:20:54.861 --> 00:20:56.515
Stupid Delta shift
stabbed us in the back

00:20:56.559 --> 00:20:59.083
and left us in a puddle
of Minooki water.

00:20:59.126 --> 00:21:01.477
Hey, check it out.
It's draining.

00:21:01.520 --> 00:21:04.349
Oh, great. I'll put that
fun detail in my personal log,

00:21:04.393 --> 00:21:05.829
right after the part
where we got betrayed.

00:21:05.872 --> 00:21:07.352
This might bypass the vent.

00:21:07.396 --> 00:21:09.833
- Uh, it's not on the map.
- Ah, I don't know.

00:21:09.876 --> 00:21:11.617
There could be incinerators
down there.

00:21:11.661 --> 00:21:13.140
Huh. Doesn't feel hot.
I guess

00:21:13.184 --> 00:21:15.229
it'll take someone bold
to find out.

00:21:15.273 --> 00:21:16.970
Boimler, no,
that's a bad idea, man.

00:21:17.014 --> 00:21:19.016
- Antigrav Boy!
- No, no, no! Boimler, no!

00:21:19.059 --> 00:21:21.192
I'm fine. It was fun.
Come on in.

00:21:21.235 --> 00:21:23.237
We really need to do something

00:21:23.281 --> 00:21:26.676
about this bold Boimler thing.
It is not sustainable.

00:21:26.719 --> 00:21:30.027
-  All right.
- Aah!

00:21:30.070 --> 00:21:33.073
- Ooh! That was fun!
- Yeah, and this

00:21:33.117 --> 00:21:35.249
goes right up to the terminal.
We're right there.

00:21:35.293 --> 00:21:36.642
And no Delta shifters in sight.

00:21:36.686 --> 00:21:39.428
Yup, 'cause fortune
favors the bold.

00:21:39.471 --> 00:21:41.386
Don't.
Don't, with the bold thing.

00:21:45.477 --> 00:21:47.436
I can't believe we did it.

00:21:47.479 --> 00:21:49.438
Joke's on them
for leaving us behind.

00:21:49.481 --> 00:21:51.091
Now there's no way
we're sharing.

00:21:51.135 --> 00:21:52.876
Just gonna make sure our names
are the only ones

00:21:52.919 --> 00:21:55.182
on the list,
then lock the Deltas out.

00:21:55.226 --> 00:21:57.141
Oh, no, no,
no, no, no, no, no, no.

00:21:57.184 --> 00:21:59.099
This says there aren't
four rooms on Deck One.

00:21:59.143 --> 00:22:01.667
- It's one room on Deck Four.
- Only one?

00:22:01.711 --> 00:22:03.843
So wait, so wait.
So who should get it?

00:22:03.887 --> 00:22:06.411
It would mean being on a
different deck, all by yourself.

00:22:06.455 --> 00:22:08.935
We wouldn't get
to have days like this anymore.

00:22:08.979 --> 00:22:11.460
Even with all the peril, it was
really fun just being together.

00:22:11.503 --> 00:22:13.113
Yeah, and you know

00:22:13.157 --> 00:22:15.246
we're only gonna
be lower deckers for so long.

00:22:15.289 --> 00:22:17.422
I mean, in no time Tendi's
gonna be a bridge officer.

00:22:17.466 --> 00:22:19.119
I'll probably get drummed
out of Starfleet

00:22:19.163 --> 00:22:20.991
for calling Ransom a piece
of [bleep], and, Boimler,

00:22:21.034 --> 00:22:23.297
you'll be dead, because
of the whole being bold thing.

00:22:23.341 --> 00:22:26.910
If even one of us takes that
room, it'll break us up forever.

00:22:26.953 --> 00:22:29.347
And you know
who really deserves that?

00:22:29.391 --> 00:22:31.262
Delta shift.

00:22:31.305 --> 00:22:33.438
Yeah. Let's just walk away and
let them ruin their friendship.

00:22:35.353 --> 00:22:36.876
Beta shifters stick together.

00:22:36.920 --> 00:22:40.793
Stupid Delta shift.

00:22:40.837 --> 00:22:42.752
Yeah, yeah, come check out
the room, everybody.

00:22:42.795 --> 00:22:44.536
- Yeah, come on by. It's huge.

00:22:44.580 --> 00:22:46.799
I can't believe
they're sharing that one room.

00:22:46.843 --> 00:22:48.801
God, they just put four beds
in there,

00:22:48.845 --> 00:22:50.412
and now it's like
their private party quarters.

00:22:50.455 --> 00:22:52.065
Ugh.
Why didn't &lt;i&gt;we&lt;/i&gt; think of that?

00:22:52.109 --> 00:22:53.676
I don't know. We were tired.

00:22:53.719 --> 00:22:55.678
Hey, why didn't you guys
grab that room for me?

00:22:55.721 --> 00:22:57.375
We didn't think
you would want it.

00:22:57.419 --> 00:22:59.072
Of course I wanted it.
What are you talking about?

00:22:59.116 --> 00:23:00.465
We all wanted it.

00:23:00.509 --> 00:23:01.684
'Cause, you know,
Beta shifters stick together.

00:23:01.727 --> 00:23:03.250
- We still could have.
- Well, we kind of

00:23:03.294 --> 00:23:05.427
got caught up in the
all-for-one, one-for-all spirit.

00:23:05.470 --> 00:23:07.559
Ugh! That's the definition
of one-for-all.

00:23:07.603 --> 00:23:09.431
One room for all of us.

00:23:09.474 --> 00:23:11.215
- Hey, hey, relax, man.
- I am relaxed!

00:23:11.258 --> 00:23:13.739
I just got back from a spa!
Listen, I heard

00:23:13.783 --> 00:23:16.176
that Delta shift is having
a private party tonight,

00:23:16.220 --> 00:23:17.308
and we got to get on that list.

00:23:17.351 --> 00:23:18.483
We could go back
to the terminal.

00:23:18.527 --> 00:23:19.789
No.

00:23:19.832 --> 00:23:21.181
- Come on. You said it was fun.
- Not that fun.

00:23:21.225 --> 00:23:23.270
Hey, how's it going? Okay.

00:23:23.314 --> 00:23:27.013
Computer, 35 churros
in an unmarked paper bag, hot.

00:24:34.341 --> 00:24:34.646
Chirp.
